//! Exception introspection helpers.
//!
//! This file is a thin wrapper around the runtime's stack unwinding support,
//! giving Kyte code a way to capture a human-readable trace of the current
//! call stack. It sits alongside the language's `try`/`catch`/`errdefer`
//! error model as a diagnostic aid: it does not throw or handle exceptions
//! itself, it only reports where the program currently is.

/// Captures the current call stack as a formatted, human-readable string.
///
/// Delegates to the native runtime (`kyte_get_stacktrace`), so the exact
/// formatting and the amount of detail available (symbol names, file/line
/// information) depend on the host platform and how the binary was built.
pub fn stackTrace(): string {
    return kyte_get_stacktrace();
}
